{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"IMPLEMENTED and PUSHED as Gerrit 1900 (patch set 2), Change-Id Ic07c25d9. LLM-Review +1 on PS1; CI running on PS2. New binding_recovery.py 411 LOC; binding_store.py 561 -> 530; binding_lifecycle.py 535 (docstring only).\n\nORDERING CORRECTION MADE BEFORE EARNING THE ATTESTATION. The story plan and this task's original impact set named run_differs.py as the invocation file for S3 T2, and the epic's constraint list asked for recovery \"after configuration snapshot/preflight ... but before remote issue fetch\". Verified against the spine: reconcile._load_snapshots (called at reconcile.py:222) constructs the store (:280), runs the under-lock staleness gate (:281-282), and performs the FIRST remote fetch (:328-333), while bind_operation_runtime is composed at :227 — AFTER _load_snapshots returns, hence after that fetch — and run_differs() is invoked at :231, also after it. So the requested conjunction is an EMPTY window, and no point inside run_differs.py can precede remote observation. Pre-observation is the load-bearing half (its purpose is to stop a pass interleaving new liveness evidence with completion), so the snapshot conjunct was dropped and the invocation moves to reconcile.py. Corrected the story plan + file_impact FIRST, then ran review-plan: PASS, signed, 0 blocking. The real size constraint is therefore reconcile.py at 795/800 — FIVE lines — not run_differs.py's 61.\n\nHELD-OUT TDD. 42 oracles authored RED-first against a signature-only scaffold; a bare ImportError was rejected as invalid RED, so the scaffold carries real signatures and the RED is 35 NotImplementedError failures with 6 correctly-green characterization/guard tests. The implementer saw 16; 26 discriminators were held outside the worktree and ALL passed unseen — the eight-case mismatch table, the write-counting idempotency oracles, replace-failure rollback, corrupt-retired fail-open, and tombstone authority against clear_absent and a same-key confirm. Implementer: 1 attempt per part, green first run.\n\nMUTATION FOUND ONE REAL ORACLE GAP, the same shape as S2 T1's and the fourth of this epic: replacing the targeted reverse pop with a SWEEP keyed on local_id stayed GREEN across all 41 tests, because every fixture had exactly one reverse key per local id. Closed with an out-of-band reverse orphan the forward entry never named — a targeted pop leaves it, a sweep takes it. Pinning the orphan's SURVIVAL is characterization not endorsement: no one-to-one forward/reverse invariant is claimed, which is why unbind carries its own orphan sweep and why bridge fsck reports reverse_missing_forward. All 8 seeded mutations now RED (rule-1 silence, dropped reverse-mismatch check, unconditional save, tombstone consumption, missing rollback, the sweep, check reordering, classifier impurity).\n\nTHE IMPLEMENTER FOUND A GENUINE TEST DEFECT AND REFUSED TO EDIT IT, correctly. test_dc_live_oracles_discriminate_5200.py asserts the colon-form label by grepping SOURCE TEXT keyed on FILE NAME, and its own docstring named \"binding_store.py:706 (pending-binding recovery)\" as the third writer — so any faithful implementation of this move fails it. I retargeted the census to binding_recovery.py myself (I own the tests), verified by grep that exactly three production writers of f\"rebar-id:{local_id}\" remain and no hyphen-form write exists anywhere, and dropped the already-stale per-writer line numbers rather than refreshing them.\n\nTWO FALSE DOCSTRINGS CORRECTED: binding_lifecycle claimed recovery \"stays with BindingStore\", and the census above. TWO BEHAVIOURS PINNED AS THEY REALLY ARE against wording implying otherwise: a corrupt LIVE store cannot yield a safety abort (it fails CLOSED in the loader, so construction raises and repair is unreachable — the reachable corrupt-live case is a malformed ENTRY SHAPE, which parses and does reach the classifier); a corrupt RETIRED file fails OPEN, so tombstones go invisible and yield no candidate, making the consequence a missed repair rather than a guessed deletion.\n\nTHREE LLM-REVIEW ADVISORIES APPLIED, not deferred, all strengthening oracles: the replace-failure evidence carried repr(exc) that no test read (now pinned to the fault text, not just the category); the facade's three grace/age aliases had nothing holding them to the recovery module's objects, so a copy could let is_keyless_pending_within_grace and the unbind conjunction drift apart silently (identity test added); and the source-grep census now cross-references its behavioural twin. Both new assertions mutation-verified RED.\n\nPROCESS. Rebased onto origin/main d361eb28e4 (RP-04 C3a-CORE) with one conflict, in generated docs/env-vars.md, resolved by taking main's copy and regenerating. That file went stale AGAIN from a two-line docstring shift moving binding_lifecycle's non-literal env read 70 -> 72 — third time in this epic, caught pre-push by the checklist this time. rebar review-code still cannot preview locally: it returns runner \"code-review-disabled\" because verify.enable_code_review is off and there is no env override, so the surface-parity census in the commit message remains the mitigation. Commit-msg hook also enforces a 50-char subject, not just the 72-column body.\n\nGATES: 3373 passed / 9 skipped (tests/unit/rebar_reconciler + tests/interfaces/store + the comment-hygiene guard); 11671 passed / 53 skipped across the whole tests/unit tree pre-rebase; lint clean, mypy 567 files, complexity new=0 increased=0, comment hygiene, config ownership, verify-gate parity, config-check all green.\n\nDEFECT FILED: easygoing-tremendous-frogmouth (7851-e06b-9e85-4c9e) discovered_from the S3 story — preview and dry-run passes perform remote add_label/set_entity_property writes during create recovery, because that call's only guard is `if not scoped_ids` and it is handed the real configured transport, while the invariant-filing gate immediately beside it composes both axes. This task's AC6 pins that gate unchanged rather than fixing it."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787142033308912001,"uuid":"bd5dc0a4-ee85-4b40-bcdd-ea4e459f70b9"}